      "id": "claim_93274b1ec6254364bcc9f9317e737216",
      "statement": "Docker images can be built directly from your Maven or Gradle plugin using Cloud Native Buildpacks. If you’ve ever used an application platform such as Cloud Foundry or Heroku then you’ve probably used a buildpack. Buildpacks are the part of the platform that takes your application and converts it into something that the platform can actually run. For example, Cloud Foundry’s Java buildpack will notice that you’re pushing a .jar file and automatically add a relevant JRE.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://upstream/documentation/spring-boot-docs/src/docs/antora/modules/reference/pages/packaging/container-images/cloud-native-buildpacks.adoc#L1-L19",
